      <p>You can schedule a virtual machine (VM) on a node if the VM CPU model and policy are supported by the node.</p>
      <h2 id="virt-about-node-labeling-obsolete-cpu-models_virt-managing-node-labeling-obsolete-cpu-models" class="group scroll-mt-20">About node labeling for obsolete CPU models<a href="#virt-about-node-labeling-obsolete-cpu-models_virt-managing-node-labeling-obsolete-cpu-models" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">The OpenShift Virtualization Operator uses a predefined list of obsolete CPU models to ensure that a node supports only valid CPU models for scheduled VMs.</p>
      <p>By default, the following CPU models are eliminated from the list of labels generated for the node:</p>
      <Fragment set:html={"<details>\n<summary>Obsolete CPU models</summary>\n"} />
      <CodeBlock code={"\"486\"\nConroe\nathlon\ncore2duo\ncoreduo\nkvm32\nkvm64\nn270\npentium\npentium2\npentium3\npentiumpro\nphenom\nqemu32\nqemu64"} lang="plaintext" />
      <Fragment set:html={"</details>\n"} />
      <p>This predefined list is not visible in the <code>HyperConverged</code> CR. You cannot <em>remove</em> CPU models from this list, but you can add to the list by editing the <code>spec.obsoleteCPUs.cpuModels</code> field of the <code>HyperConverged</code> CR.</p>
      <h2 id="virt-configuring-obsolete-cpu-models_virt-managing-node-labeling-obsolete-cpu-models" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring obsolete CPU models<a href="#virt-configuring-obsolete-cpu-models_virt-managing-node-labeling-obsolete-cpu-models" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can configure a list of obsolete CPU models by editing the <code>HyperConverged</code> custom resource (CR).</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Edit the <code>HyperConverged</code> custom resource, specifying the obsolete CPU models in the <code>obsoleteCPUs</code> array. For example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: hco.kubevirt.io/v1beta1\nkind: HyperConverged\nmetadata:\n  name: kubevirt-hyperconverged\n  namespace: {{ CNVNamespace }}\nspec:\n  obsoleteCPUs:\n    cpuModels:\n      - \"<obsolete_cpu_1>\"\n      - \"<obsolete_cpu_2>\""} lang="yaml" />
      <p>Replace the example values in the <code>cpuModels</code> array with obsolete CPU models. Any value that you specify is added to a predefined list of obsolete CPU models. The predefined list is not visible in the CR.</p>
